      "Most pitcher filters on store shelves are optimized for one thing: making tap water taste better. The ClearWell Pro Lead Shield is built around a different goal entirely, and it shows. Its multi-stage cartridge combines activated carbon block with an ion-exchange resin layer specifically engineered to bind lead, and the company backs that claim with independent NSF/ANSI 53 certification for lead reduction plus NSF/ANSI 401 certification covering a list of emerging contaminants that includes several PFAS compounds. That distinction matters more than most shoppers realize. A huge share of pitchers on the market only carry NSF/ANSI 42, the standard that covers chlorine taste and odor and essentially nothing else. Over four months we ran ClearWell's cartridge against tap water from three different municipal sources and one well with known iron content, and it consistently produced the cleanest lab strip readings of any pitcher we tested for both lead and general hardness-adjacent metals. The tradeoff is speed. Water moves through the dense filter media slowly, so a full 10-cup reservoir takes close to 12 minutes to drain, noticeably longer than the mainstream brands. We consider that an acceptable price for genuine removal rather than marketing removal. The cartridge is rated for 100 gallons, which puts it mid-pack on lifespan but ahead of the pack on what it actually pulls out of your water. If you've had a lead test come back positive, or you simply want your filter dollars going toward measurable contaminant reduction rather than better-tasting water, this is our top recommendation without much competition.",
  },
  {
    id: "brightspring-classic",
    name: "BrightSpring Classic Everyday Pitcher",
    category: "Activated Carbon (Taste & Odor)",
    badge: "Most Popular Brand",
    amazonUrl: "#",
    rating: 4.4,
    reviewCount: 24800,
    pros: [
      "Widely available at every grocery store and pharmacy in the country",
      "Filters and replacement cartridges are the cheapest to find on short notice",
      "NSF/ANSI 42 certified for chlorine taste and odor reduction",
      "Simple, no-fuss design that fits most refrigerator door shelves",
      "Filter change reminder sticker built into the lid",
